Beat my track modifications (2026-11-09): exterior simplified offline into two
mesh tiers; geometry split into paint, glazing, trim, hood, aero, lamps and wheels;
source studio, rig, animation, embedded texture maps, badges and cabin floor
removed; native opaque windows and native game materials replace source shaders;
rim geometry aligned with the existing Super rally contacts; existing native
round tyre geometry replaces the source tyre meshes. Existing native
game cosmetic parts adapted to the new exterior. No runtime rig or interior.

Surface refinement (2026-11-09): door skins and hood rebuilt as smooth surfaces;
door seams, handles and fuel door represented by flush contour markings;
bonnet vents made flush, nose extended slightly, tiny exterior details removed
and glazing backing inset to remove overlapping surface artefacts.

Exterior detail refinement (2026-11-12): authored projector optics and light
guides, open-cell grille, smoked rear applique and rolled exhaust tips replace
fragile source details. Shallow bonnet vents replace flat markings. New native
split-spoke factory wheels, rounder tyres, coherent opaque glazing normals and
revised automotive paint/glass finishes improve close views. Interior remains
removed; door, handle and fuel-cap markings remain flush.

